        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Black Friday is usually a strong time to buy a treadmill</strong>,
            but the deal is the delivered price against what the machine actually sold for — not
            the percentage on the badge. Genuine reductions typically land around 15 to 30% off the
            normal selling price.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Shortlist two or three machines, record their prices in October, and buy whichever meets
            your ceiling once delivery, bundles and return terms are counted. If nothing does,
            <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the second half of January</a>
            is the next good window.
          </p>
